@chapter 24 | Plant Physiology

@intro
This chapter is about how plants live: **photosynthesis** (chlorophyll and magnesium, the source of oxygen, red light, algae), **transport** (xylem and phloem), **mineral nutrition** (nitrate, micronutrients, nitrogen, sulphur and boron), **plant hormones** (auxin, gibberellin, cytokinin, abscisic acid, ethylene) and **crop practices** (air layering, hybrid seed, crop rotation, clonal selection, hydroponics). It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 24.1 | Photosynthesis

@q 47:1-2

**Chlorophyll** has a **magnesium** atom at the centre of its porphyrin ring (haemoglobin has iron at the same position). The overall reaction is 6CO_{2} + 12H_{2}O + light → C_{6}H_{12}O_{6} + 6O_{2} + 6H_{2}O.

