@src 47:5
@pyq U.P. R.O./A.R.O. (Mains) 2014
Oxygen, which is liberated during photosynthesis, comes from :
(a) Water
(b) Carbon dioxide
(c) Chlorophyll
(d) Phosphoglyceric acid
@ans (a)
@end

The oxygen given off comes from **splitting water** (photolysis), shown by Ruben and Kamen with the isotope O-18; the carbon and the oxygen of sugar come from CO_{2}.

